Conformance
Id	Clause
conformance.1	This specification defines one class of product, a reader, which reads a Messages API request and its response [ANTHROPIC-API] and writes the attributes of the event that records the call, gen_ai.client.inference.operation.details [OTEL-GENAI]. The event itself is written by the specification of the product that recorded the call.
conformance.2	A reader conforms if, for every request and response, it writes each attribute of the Attributes sheet by the rules the sheet names for it, and no other, and if it rejects every request and response it must reject.
conformance.3	The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [BCP14] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
conformance.4	The Rules and the Attributes are normative. The first part of a rule's Id names what it governs: event the event's attributes, request the request, response the response, block a content block. A rule names each source it follows in brackets, as [ANTHROPIC-API]; the References list them, each marked normative or informative. This specification has no optional features: where a source leaves a choice to the implementation, a rule closes it.
conformance.5	Request, response, message, content block and tool are as defined in [ANTHROPIC-API]; event, attribute, part and definition as in [OTEL-GENAI]; requirement level as in [OTEL-SEMCONV]; instrumentation library as in [OTEL-GLOSSARY]; member, name and value as in [RFC8259]; property as in [JSON-SCHEMA-07]. A member is consumed when a rule writes it under a name of its own; the rest of an object are its members not consumed. In the Attributes sheet, Key is an attribute's key or, inside one of the four structured attributes, a definition's name as the living-memory specification's Sheets write it; Field is a property of that definition, additionalProperties naming the rest; Rule names the rules that write it, or that state why it is absent.
Rules
Id	Rule
event.1	gen_ai.operation.name MUST be chat, the well-known value for a chat completion operation, and gen_ai.provider.name anthropic [OTEL-GENAI].
event.2	A reader writes the attributes of event.1, and each other attribute whose value the request and response hold, by the living-memory specification's event.2, spec/living-memory.mtsv. A request or response that was not recorded is not held, and a reader MUST write none of its attributes.
event.3	These attributes of the event are absent, and a reader MUST NOT write them: the Messages API request has no seed, choice count, frequency or presence penalty, prompt template or previous response, and its usage no count by modality [ANTHROPIC-API]. gen_ai.tool.call.arguments and gen_ai.tool.call.result are attributes of the execute tool span, gen_ai.memory.records of the memory span and gen_ai.retrieval.documents of the retrieval span, not of this event [OTEL-GENAI]: the Messages API holds a call's tool use and its result inside the messages, written by block.5 and block.6, and holds no memory records or retrieval documents [ANTHROPIC-API].
event.4	Each attribute takes its Value Type, and every other value its AnyValue, by the living-memory specification's event.3; the members of an object of the request or response that share a name are read by its event.4.
event.5	A request or response is non-conforming by the living-memory specification's event.6, and so is a message without a role or a content, or a response without a role or a content [ANTHROPIC-API]; a reader MUST reject it [RFC9413].
event.6	A reader MUST write gen_ai.conversation.compacted, true, when a message of the request holds a compaction block, or the response's stop_reason is compaction, its content holds a compaction block or its usage's iterations an entry of type compaction, as the reference implementation does; otherwise it is absent, and never false [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-SDK]. The compaction blocks themselves are written by block.9.
request.1	A reader MUST write the request's model as gen_ai.request.model, max_tokens as gen_ai.request.max_tokens, temperature as gen_ai.request.temperature, top_k as gen_ai.request.top_k, top_p as gen_ai.request.top_p and stop_sequences as gen_ai.request.stop_sequences, as the request holds them [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API]; and stream as gen_ai.request.stream only when it is true, an unset attribute meaning the request is not streaming, so that a stream of false and no stream are both unset [OTEL-GENAI].
request.2	A reader MUST write output_config's effort as gen_ai.request.reasoning.level, the exact string sent [OTEL-GENAI]; and, when output_config holds a format, gen_ai.output.type json, the value for a JSON object of known or unknown schema [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API]. The rest of output_config, the format included, is written by request.6.
request.3	A reader MUST write messages as gen_ai.input.messages, in the order sent [OTEL-GENAI]: for each message a chat message, its role the message's role as written, and its parts: for a content that is a string, one text part holding it; for a content that is an array, one part for each content block, in order, by the block rules. A message has no name [ANTHROPIC-API], so a chat message's name is absent; the rest of a message are the chat message's own members [OTEL-GENAI].
request.4	A reader MUST write system as gen_ai.system_instructions: for a string, one text part holding it; for an array, one part for each block, by the block rules, a text block by block.2 [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
request.5	A reader MUST write tools as gen_ai.tool.definitions: a client tool, whose type is custom or absent, and which has a name, a function tool definition requiring one [OTEL-GENAI], as a function tool definition, its type function, its name and description the tool's, and its input_schema as parameters, the rest of the tool its own members; and any other tool, a server tool or a client tool without a name, as the request holds it, a definition with a type and a name of its own [ANTHROPIC-API] [OTEL-GENAI]. An input_schema is a JSON Schema of draft 2020-12, and parameters one of draft-07; it is written as the request holds it, and the living-memory specification validates it against draft-07 [OTEL-GENAI] [JSON-SCHEMA-07]. Description and parameters are not populated by default [OTEL-GENAI]; a reader writes them, the request being written whole.
request.6	A reader MUST write every other member of the request, and the rest of output_config, as anthropic.request.{member} [OTEL-SEMCONV] [OTEL-GENAI].
response.1	A reader MUST write the response's id as gen_ai.response.id, model as gen_ai.response.model, and stop_reason as gen_ai.response.finish_reasons, a list of the one stop_reason as written, a response being one choice [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
response.2	A reader MUST write, of usage, input_tokens plus cache_creation_input_tokens plus cache_read_input_tokens, those that are numbers, as gen_ai.usage.input_tokens; cache_read_input_tokens as gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens as gen_ai.usage.cache_write.input_tokens, output_tokens as gen_ai.usage.output_tokens, and output_tokens_details' thinking_tokens as gen_ai.usage.reasoning.output_tokens, each when it is a number [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API]. The rest of usage is written by response.4.
response.3	A reader MUST write content as gen_ai.output.messages: one output message, its role the response's role as written, and its parts one for each content block, in order, by the block rules [OTEL-GENAI]. A response has no name [ANTHROPIC-API], so the output message's name is absent; its finish_reason is deprecated, the finish reasons being written by response.1, and is absent [OTEL-GENAI].
response.4	A reader MUST write every other member of the response, and the rest of usage, as anthropic.response.{member} [OTEL-SEMCONV] [OTEL-GENAI].
block.1	A reader MUST write a content block as the part a rule names only when the block holds every member that part requires [OTEL-GENAI] [JSON-SCHEMA-07]; otherwise block.9 writes it. The members a rule consumes are written under the part's names, and the rest of the block are the part's own members [OTEL-GENAI].
block.2	A text block is a text part, its text as content [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.3	An image or a document block is a part of modality image or document: with a source of type base64, a blob part, the source's media_type as mime_type and its data, base64, as content; with a source of type url, a uri part, its url as uri; with a source of type file, a file part, its file_id as file_id; the rest of the source, if any, is the part's member source. A uri or file part has no mime_type, the source holding none. A document whose source is of type text or content is written by block.9, its data not being base64 [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.4	A thinking block is a reasoning part, its thinking as content [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.5	A tool_use block is a tool_call part, its id as id, its name as name and its input as arguments [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.6	A tool_result block is a tool_call_response part, its tool_use_id as id and its content as response; a tool_result block without content is written by block.9, response being required [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.7	A server_tool_use block is a server_tool_call part, its id as id, its name as name, and as server_tool_call an object whose type is the block's name and whose input is the block's input [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.8	A web_search_tool_result, web_fetch_tool_result, code_execution_tool_result, bash_code_execution_tool_result, text_editor_code_execution_tool_result or tool_search_tool_result block is a server_tool_call_response part, its tool_use_id as id, and as server_tool_call_response an object whose type is the block's type and whose content is the block's content [OTEL-GENAI] [ANTHROPIC-API].
block.9	A reader MUST write any other content block, and a block block.1 sends here, whole, as the request or response holds it: a part whose type is the block's type, which the living-memory specification reads by the definition that type names, or as generic [OTEL-GENAI].
